# What does a shift-and-add multiply cost on the card?  (ledger #1574; for the maths-side decision, S_CORE_TODO.md section G)
# Three single-job runs of the vgain program (it multiplies by shift and add), each alone on one block, at no fusion (lw 0) and 32 lanes fused (lw 5),
# each run twice (the first run after a load can be slower).  Needs the hk build on the card (hj has the lw 5 defect: for hj change the two `set lw 5` to `set lw 4`).
#   A: 40 words, gain 255 (all multiplier bits set)   B: 80 words, gain 255   C: 80 words, gain 1 (almost no multiply work)
# Each run prints "block 0 ... N clocks".  Then:  python3 mul_cost_calc_v1.py A_CLOCKS B_CLOCKS C_CLOCKS   (for lw 0 and again for lw 5)
# Run it:  batch batches/mul_cost.score     (in the shell or in the window)
use hk8s32u32n1i1024
set blocks 1
set linkcheck on
# ---- no fusion, lw 0
set lw 0
new
add vgain seq 1000 40 1 arg=255
run
run
new
add vgain seq 1000 80 1 arg=255
run
run
new
add vgain seq 1000 80 1 arg=1
run
run
# ---- 32 lanes fused, lw 5
set lw 5
new
add vgain seq 1000 40 1 arg=255
run
run
new
add vgain seq 1000 80 1 arg=255
run
run
new
add vgain seq 1000 80 1 arg=1
run
run
